      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "| Threads | VNNI (Project Zero) | LUT (lut_mm) | Speedup |\n|--------:|--------------------:|-------------:|--------:|\n| 1       | 34.15               | 42.66       | 1.25×   |\n| 2       | 47.43               | 51.11        | 1.08×   |\n| 4       | 48.09               | 51.93        | 1.08×   |\n| 8       | 48.40               | 52.13        | 1.08×   |\n| 16      | 52.96              | 56.66        | 1.07×   |\n\ntok/s microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T\non my AMD 9950x\n\nI had Claude run Project Zero with VNNI on my PC. I then had it plug in my 5 activation LUT method into project zero. The denser weight format might be useful to play with. My old PC only has a Intel 6700k from like 10 years ago, so I can't test on Intel right now. Maybe, you can try the 5 bit lookup table on your hardware to see if it beats the VNNI method?\n\nFrom what I understand, Intel and AMD might have pretty different performance characteristics for advanced instructions.",
