      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Ah, good to know. Our Xeon showed 1.16x anyway - floor not ceiling for what LUT can do vs a properly optimized VNNI path.\n\nBut the number I'm actually curious about: when Claude ran inference with your LUT patch in PZ, what tok/s came out? Kernel Gop/s is useful but pipeline overhead, activation quant path, batch shaping - all of that eats into the margin, and end-to-end inference tok/s is the only number that actually matters for someone trying to decide which path to use.",
