      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Ah, missed that - so your table was actual inference tok/s on the 9950X. VNNI (PZ) 34.15 → LUT 42.66 at T=1, 1.25x end-to-end. More useful than kernel Gop/s.\n\nK-6 is integrated on our side now. The situation on our Xeon 8259CL (AVX-512BW, no VNNI) is different from the 1.16x we reported on that cloud Xeon with VNNI:\n\n| kernel | Gop/s | vs float32 |\n|--------|-------|------------|\n| AVX-512F float32 | 2.5 | 1.00x |\n| LUT AVX-512BW | 74.6 | 29.3x |\n\nOn hardware without VNNI, float32 was the ternary kernel ceiling before K-6. 29.3x kernel vs 1.16x on VNNI hardware - different situations entirely.\n\nEnd-to-end tok/s pending - blocked on model availability on this machine (disk). Will update once we have it.",
